|name = Berserkory
|image = E 206.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[Revolving-door Floats|Sub-chapter 26 - Revolving-door Floats]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Nonsense Mutation|Sub-chapter 13 - Nonsense Mutation]]
|money drop = 900¢ - 3,555¢
}}

==Enemy==
Berserkory acts almost the same as his original form, performing a medium-strength attack and firing a [[Wave Attack]]. However, the Wave Attack range has been tripled, so few Cats can avoid it. He only has one knockback and very high health, causing even more Wave Attacks if you don't use any [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red Cats]]. Luckily, he has lower range and movement speed, not to mention the lack of Base Destroyer.

==Strategy==
Despite the waves, there are several units who can easily stall this enemy. [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], for example, has no issue keeping Berserkory at a standstill, especially if they succeed in weakening him. Other units who can stall and wear down Berserkory include [[Viking Cat (Rare Cat)|Maximum the Fighter]], [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|and]] [[Li'l Fish Cat (Special Cat)|variants]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Ultimate Bondage Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], or [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Dread Pirate Catley]] (especially if Talented), to name a few. When relying on Maximum and/or Islands, make sure to use [[Cat Combo]]s like [[Seasons of Love (Combo)|Seasons of Love]] and [[Three Kings (Combo)|Three Kings]] for extra tankiness. You can also deal some serious damage to Berserkory with [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], but do note that Berserkory can infiltrate his blindspot, so make sure to bring extra support for Courier to kill Berserkory.

If you have [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]], then deploy two of them out of sync. Because of Berserkory's low range and singular knockback, it's very easy to perma-freeze him on his own, making him extremely easy to defeat. Pairing units that can disable Reds like iCat with [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] such as [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] and [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]] can further reduce his pushing power, as they'll simply stop his wave attacks.

